Expected merge conflicts at orchestrator integration time:

- `server.go` (W3A territory): W3A's seed defines a stub
  `newDeclarationService(*declaration.Manager) *declarationService` with a
  `TODO(W3B)` marker. **Orchestrator should keep THIS branch's
  declaration.go (real impl)**; the stub in server.go is dropped (the
  symbol resolves to declaration.go after merge). If W3A's stub is in
  server.go itself, no conflict — both sides compile because
  declarationService is defined exactly once in declaration.go.
- `errs.go`: W3A and/or W3C may also define `errs.go`. Orchestrator
  picks one canonical version — they should have the same shape (sentinel
  -> status mapping per docs/idd.md §1.1.4). If they diverge, the union
  of all sentinel cases is the safe choice.
- `object.go` / `stream.go` (W3C territory): no overlap with this
  branch's owned files.

